Subject: [PATCH] classobject: method.__get__ returns the bound method again

CPython 3.11 and 3.12 removed tp_descr_get from PyMethod_Type. A bound method's
__get__ then falls through to the function's __get__, so
bound.__get__(None, owner) returns the bare function instead of the bound method.
Ren'Py 7 game code calls that form (hasattr(v, '__get__') then v.__get__(None, self)),
and it fails with a missing-argument TypeError during init.

Restore the 3.9 and 3.13 behavior: method objects return themselves from __get__.
Upstream: python/cpython d058eaeed4 (gh-113157, gh-89519, gh-113233).

---
--- a/Objects/classobject.c
+++ b/Objects/classobject.c
@@ -318,6 +318,13 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
+static PyObject *
+method_descr_get(PyObject *meth, PyObject *obj, PyObject *cls)
+{
+    Py_INCREF(meth);
+    return meth;
+}
+
 PyTypeObject PyMethod_Type = {
     PyVarObject_HEAD_INIT(&PyType_Type, 0)
     .tp_name = "method",
@@ -338,6 +345,7 @@
     .tp_methods = method_methods,
     .tp_members = method_memberlist,
     .tp_getset = method_getset,
+    .tp_descr_get = method_descr_get,
     .tp_new = method_new,
 };
 
